  "title": "BGP: Fix false positive in add-path detection",
  "description": "The `detect_add_path_prefix46()` function incorrectly used 'end - offset' instead of 'end - o' when checking for remaining bytes after a /0 prefix.\nThis caused NLRIs containing default route (0.0.0.0/0) to be misidentified as add-path format, resulting in malformed packet errors.\n\n[bgp.pcap](/uploads/9348068285b28c74357b99699e2dc47e/bgp.pcap)",
